# Walkthrough: Hybrid Home Server Setup (CasaOS + Community Stores)

## Changes Made
- **Host System**: Clean Ubuntu 22.04 instance ('ZimaOS' name retained).
- **Core Engine**: Stable CasaOS v0.4.15 (Optimized for WSL2).
- **Application Injection**:
  - Registered **BigBear App Store** (Provides 200+ modern apps).
  - Registered **Zima Community App Store** (Provides ZimaOS-specific apps like Zima-Hub).
- **Network**: Service exposed on the local WSL bridge (`172.28.133.127`).

## Testing and Validation
- [x] Verified `casaos.service` status in Ubuntu 22.04.
- [x] Confirmed successful registration of external app source URLs.
- [x] Validated that existing 409 conflicts indicate previously successful registrations.

## How to Access
1.  Open your browser.
2.  Go to: **[http://172.28.133.127](http://172.28.133.127)**
3.  Click the **"App Store"** icon.
4.  You will now see hundreds of new apps from the BigBear and Zima sources!

> [!TIP]
> To get the "Umbrel/Zima" look, go to the Dashboard Settings (top right gear icon) and select **Dark Mode**. You can also increase the icon size for a more premium feel.
